# deploy/.env.example -- copy to deploy/.env, fill in, chmod 600. See docs/bring-up.md 6.
#
#     cd /srv/wow/wowserver/deploy
#     cp -n .env.example .env
#     chmod 600 .env
#
# TWO parsers read this file: Compose's own .env reader, and `sh`, when scripts/backup.sh,
# scripts/soap-cmd.sh and bring-up.md 6's one-liners do `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`.
# They agree only on plain KEY=value:
#
#     no quotes            no `export`            no spaces around `=`
#     no shell expansions  no trailing comments   one line per value
#
# A value Compose takes literally but `sh` re-expands is a password mismatch you will
# debug as "access denied".
#
# GENERATE BOTH PASSWORDS FROM [A-Za-z0-9] ONLY, and this whole class of problem is gone:
#
#     LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9' < /dev/urandom | head -c 32; echo
#
# Three characters in particular are load-bearing to avoid:
#   #   starts a comment mid-line inside a MySQL option file, so it would truncate
#       MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD where scripts/backup.sh writes it into mysql-backup.cnf.
#   \   is still read as an escape there, even when quoted.
#   ;   is the field separator in AzerothCore's "host;port;user;password;database"
#       strings, so it would split ACORE_DB_PASSWORD in half.
#
# This file is the committed template. deploy/.env itself is gitignored, and so are the
# two files generated from it: deploy/mysql-init/01-databases.sql and
# deploy/mysql-backup.cnf. All three hold a password in cleartext. Keep it that way —
# the repo is public.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by deploy/docker-compose.yml
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MySQL's root password. Generated, never typed. Used by the mysql service, and written
# by scripts/backup.sh into deploy/mysql-backup.cnf (0600) — which is where every
# mysql/mysqldump invocation in this project gets it from. It never goes on a command
# line: container processes show up in `ps` on the host.
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=

# The password for the `acore` MySQL user, i.e. what all four AzerothCore pools
# authenticate with. Generated. It is read TWICE from here and the two MUST match:
# once by `envsubst` into mysql-init/01-databases.sql (the GRANT), and once by Compose
# into the four AC_*_DATABASE_INFO connection strings. Change it after first boot and
# you must also ALTER USER inside MySQL — regenerating the init SQL does nothing,
# /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d only runs on an empty data directory.
ACORE_DB_PASSWORD=

# The GitHub user or org the image was pushed under: ghcr.io/<owner>/wowserver.
GHCR_OWNER=

# The image tag to run. A commit SHA, never `latest` and never a branch name —
# hosting.md 3.6. This is the only thing that decides which build is live.
IMAGE_TAG=

# The VPS's Tailscale address: `tailscale ip -4` on the host, a 100.x.y.z. Both game
# ports are published on this address ONLY, so nothing is reachable from the internet.
# It must also match acore_auth.realmlist.address, which is a separate manual step and
# the single most common private-server failure — hosting.md 5.2.
TAILSCALE_IP=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read by Compose. Read by scripts/soap-cmd.sh, which sources this same file.
# hosting.md 7.6 -- these are two keys beyond the five bring-up.md 5.1 tabulates.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A GM account (`.account set gmlevel <acct> 3 -1`) used to POST commands to the SOAP
# endpoint on 127.0.0.1:7878 — that is how the weekly `server restart 300` cron works
# without an interactive `docker attach`. SOAP is HTTP Basic over cleartext on loopback;
# these are not the account you play on.
AC_SOAP_USER=
AC_SOAP_PASS=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What an empty value does
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD  Compose refuses to run and prints the message. Guarded.
#   ACORE_DB_PASSWORD    Compose refuses to run and prints the message. Guarded.
#   GHCR_OWNER           Compose refuses to run and prints the message. Guarded.
#   IMAGE_TAG            Compose refuses to run and prints the message. Guarded.
#   TAILSCALE_IP         Compose refuses to run and prints the message. Guarded.
#   AC_SOAP_USER/PASS    Compose does not care; soap-cmd.sh gets a 401.
#
# DEVIATION FROM docs/bring-up.md 5.1, stated so nobody thinks it is an accident:
# that section guards only MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and IMAGE_TAG, and its table notes that
# TAILSCALE_IP is "not guarded, and it fails silently" — empty, "${TAILSCALE_IP}:8085:8085"
# becomes ":8085:8085", which Compose accepts as a publish on every interface. That is
# the exact opposite of the reason the tailnet bind exists, so the compose file guards
# all five instead. Failing loudly on a blank .env costs nothing; publishing the auth
# server to the internet because a variable was blank costs a lot.
